1391 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1390 0 R
  /Alt (Two geographic maps of an urban area in Iasi, Romania, showing the classification of Green Urban Areas (GUA) and Recreational Areas with respect to public, private, or unknown access, based on Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) Urban Atlas (UA) nomenclature extensions. Both maps display the same vector data overlay from the `ro502l1_iasi_ua2018_2021` dataset, indicated by coloured outlines, and share an identical legend and scale bar. A North arrow is present in the top right corner of each map. The top map uses an OpenStreetMap (OSM) topographic base layer, depicting streets, buildings, and green spaces. The bottom map uses high-resolution aerial or satellite imagery as its base layer, showing detailed land cover and urban infrastructure. The legend classifies polygons by their border colour: * **Blue outline (14110):** Public access areas. * **Red outline (14120):** Private access areas. * **Purple outline (14130):** Unknown access areas. * **Green outline (14200):** Recreational Areas. The scale bar indicates distances of 0, 0.1, and 0.2 km. The maps visually compare how these classified areas of different access types are situated within the urban landscape and natural surroundings, highlighting, for example, a large forested area with significant public access (blue outlines) adjacent to a stadium identified as a Recreational Area (green outline).)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 2686 0 R
>>
endobj

